USERADD(1)                  User Commands

NAME
    useradd, userdel - create and remove accounts

SYNOPSIS
    useradd [-u uid] [-g group] [-G group,...] [-c full-name] [-d home]
            [-s shell] [-M] name
    userdel [-r] name

DESCRIPTION
    useradd creates the account name. It receives the lowest uid from
    1000 on that is free, together with the same gid, unless -u gives the
    uid. A group of the account's name and gid is created unless -g names
    an existing group as the account's group. -G adds the account to the
    member lists of further groups. -c sets the full name, -s the shell
    (/bin/sh by default) and -d the home, /home/name by default, which
    useradd makes from /etc/skel with mode 0700 unless -M is given. The
    password is locked until passwd(1) sets one.

    userdel removes the account name from /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow and
    the member lists of /etc/group. Its own group goes as well when no
    other account has it as its group. -r also removes the home
    directory. root cannot be removed.

    Only root may run either command. Names start with a lowercase letter
    and continue with lowercase letters, digits, _ and -, up to 32
    characters.

EXAMPLES
    useradd -c 'Anna Example' anna
    passwd anna
    userdel -r anna

FILES
    /etc/passwd, /etc/group, /etc/shadow, /etc/skel

SEE ALSO
    passwd(1), id(1), fsinit(1), passwd(5), index(7)
